<figure class="viz" id="viz-when">
  <p class="chart-title">When, versus whether</p>
  <p class="sr-only">
    Schematic, not data. No blink amplitudes are shown. Temporal uncertainty was the largest startle. Occurrence uncertainty was larger than certain threat only. Safe was not reliably different from certain threat or from occurrence uncertainty.
  </p>
  <ul class="ordinal" aria-label="Qualitative order of anticipation startle. Schematic, not data.">
    <li>
      <div class="bar" style="--h: 4.7rem">
        <span class="rank">Tied low</span>
        <span class="cond">Certain</span>
      </div>
      <p class="bar-note">Not different from safe</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="bar range" style="--h: 7.8rem">
        <span class="rank">Not pinned</span>
        <span class="cond">Safe</span>
      </div>
      <p class="bar-note">Not different from certain or from whether</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="bar" style="--h: 7.8rem">
        <span class="rank">Higher</span>
        <span class="cond">Whether</span>
      </div>
      <p class="bar-note">Larger than certain only</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="bar" style="--h: 12.4rem">
        <span class="rank">Largest</span>
        <span class="cond">When</span>
      </div>
      <p class="bar-note">Larger than the other three</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>Schematic, not data.</strong> Bennett, Dickmann, and Larson (2018) do not print startle means or error bars; those appear only in Figure 3, so nothing here is in microvolts. Section 3.2 reports a main effect of condition during anticipation, F(3, 123) = 16.34, p &lt; .0001, partial η² = 0.285. Temporal uncertainty (when) was larger than occurrence uncertainty (whether), certain threat, and safe, ps &lt; .0001. Occurrence uncertainty was larger than certain threat, p &lt; .012, and was not larger than safe, p = .44. Certain threat and safe did not differ, p &gt; .99. The dashed safe bar spans those two non-differences instead of claiming a height.
    <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6013348/">Bennett, Dickmann, and Larson, 2018</a>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
